## Development Rules
- Inspect relevant files before editing.
- Make small isolated changes that are easy to review.
- Preserve public contracts unless the task explicitly allows contract changes.
- Follow existing naming, layout, and dependency patterns before introducing new ones.
- Update docs or comments when behavior or assumptions change.
- Record accepted architectural decisions in `docs/ai/decisions.md`.
- Keep `docs/ai/current-state.md` synchronized with meaningful implementation and verification results.
- Do not silently answer questions recorded in `docs/ai/open-questions.md`; document the evidence or owner needed to resolve them.

## Definition Of Done
- Behavior matches the requested outcome.
- Public contracts are preserved or intentionally documented.
- Tests were added or updated for changed behavior.
- Validation steps were run, or any gaps are called out explicitly.
- Risks, assumptions, and follow-up work are documented.

## AI Working Agreement
